course: dictionary
lesson: 2592
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word dentist can mean a person, or a place where that person works. The words around it, its context, show you which meaning is used. «The dentist checked my teeth and found no holes.» Checking teeth is something a person does, so dentist means the person here.
explain: «We waited in the dentist's for almost an hour.» Waited tells you people sit in a place and wait, so dentist's means the office where the dentist works. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits.
explain: Real sentences use this trick too. «Feeling nervous is normal; you can tell the dentist, ask what they will do, and agree a signal.» You tell and ask a person, so the dentist here means the person doing the work.
fact: A dentist is a doctor who looks after people's teeth and gums.
fact: A dentist checks teeth, cleans them and fixes problems such as holes.
fact: «The dentist's» can also mean the place where the dentist works, which is an office.
fact: Useful phrases: go to the dentist, dentist's appointment, check-up, filling, dental nurse.
fact: Brushing your teeth twice a day and eating less sugar means fewer problems for the dentist to fix.
exercise: «The dentist found a small hole in my tooth.» What does dentist mean here? | A sweet shop | A kind of toothbrush | A place where people wait for a bus | *A doctor who looks after teeth
exercise: «We waited in the dentist's for almost an hour.» What does dentist's mean here? | A long train journey | *The place where the dentist works | A hole in a tooth | A person who checks teeth
exercise: Which phrase means a visit to the dentist to check your teeth? | Filling | *Check-up | Dental nurse
test: «The dentist's was cold and quiet, with a row of shiny chairs.» What does dentist's mean? | *The place where the dentist works | A cold drink | A quiet park
test: Which sentence describes a dentist? | A farmer who grows apples | A teacher who teaches maths | *A doctor who looks after people's teeth and gums | A driver who takes people to work
exam: Ella reads «She sat in the dentist's, waiting for her name to be called.» How can she tell which meaning of dentist is used? | *Look at the clue words: sat and waiting show it is a place | Count the letters in the word | Skip the word and never think about it again | Guess the first meaning she thinks of and stop
